              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SilverChai3421"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy to make and finished product looked just like pictures. But they were too dense and heavy making them chewy and hard to eat. I made them about half the size and filled with my homemade jam. Not a hit in my hannukah dinner celebration.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-01T03:30:34.312Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AnnA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made it and very happy with the process and description. Quite easy to make and clearly described. I followed the recipe to a t. They came out quite dense inside. Is that how they should be? I was expecting softer, fluffier. Can someone please reply? Thanks. J",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-10T16:51:50.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeff Lambert"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I served them with powdered sugar and a side of jelly, since they usually are served jelly filled.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-29T17:15:30.053Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Wendy Lyons"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are yummy and super easy to make, but the texture and denseness are quite different than traditional sufganiyot. I made a batch of these and a batch of yeast-based sufganiyot (from an Israeli friend's recipe). I took them to a Chanukah party and asked people to vote. Every single person, including several Israelis, voted for the yeast-based donuts. It is still a good recipe for easy donuts, but it's just not the same as traditional sufganiyot.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-18T08:50:56.513Z"
          },
          {
